  "journal": {
    "entry_id": "36ccfd85672517e5887d67977fb9c34e93c39165633e53deda6d3650ffc87721",
    "text": "This session I read through the minbpe lineage to get oriented. I went over minbpe/regex.py lines 1-378, lineage_bench.py lines 1-107, minbpe/base.py lines 1-378, minbpe/basic.py lines 1-239, minbpe/__init__.py lines 1-5, and minbpe/gpt4.py lines 1-133. I made no edits.\n\nNothing was measured. I ran no sandbox evaluations, and the session stopped without submitting a candidate, so there is no result to report and nothing for replays to check.\n\nWhat I now know is the layout. The tokenizer logic is split across base.py, basic.py, regex.py and gpt4.py, and lineage_bench.py is the harness that will judge any change. I have not tested any idea about where time is spent, so I hold no belief about bottlenecks yet.\n\nNext session, I should run lineage_bench.py on the unmodified code first to get a baseline. Then I should pick one concrete change in the training or encode path, measure it in the sandbox, and only submit if the numbers support it.",
